                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width: 20%;">Challenge</th>
                        <th style="width: 40%;">Issues</th>
                        <th style="width: 40%;">Benefits of technological approach</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>2.2.1 Overcoming disjointed communication and information silos from within the mines</td>
                        <td>Many independent pieces of equipment and systems, each with its own data and interfaces.</td>
                        <td>Changes how miners view and interact with their operations and markets.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Duplicated activities and costs.</td>
                        <td>Allows greater visibility of operations by integrating disparate systems.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Different sites and departments run their own processes.</td>
                        <td>Enables real-time data exchange across the entire value chain.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Difficulty making timely, effective decisions to manage the complex, interconnected nature of modern mines.</td>
                        <td>Enables better decision making by providing a single source of truth.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <table style="font-size: 0.9em;">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width: 20%;">Challenge</th>
                        <th style="width: 40%;">Issues</th>
                        <th style="width: 40%;">Benefits of technological approach</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>2.2.2 Leveraging collaboration across the entire supply chain</td>
                        <td>Elements of the supply chain are isolated from each other.</td>
                        <td>Enables seamless collaboration across the entire value chain.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Suppliers, customers and partners rarely interact.</td>
                        <td>Allows teams to communicate and collaborate across the entire value chain.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Lack of visibility into the entire operational challenges.</td>
                        <td>Provides end-to-end visibility of the entire value chain.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Insufficient sharing of best practice.</td>
                        <td>Enables the sharing of best practices across the entire value chain.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Reinventing the wheel time and again</td>
                        <td></td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <table style="font-size: 0.9em;">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width: 20%;">Challenge</th>
                        <th style="width: 40%;">Issues</th>
                        <th style="width: 40%;">Benefits of technological approach</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>2.2.3 Managing aging assets to minimize downtime risk and its impact on profitability</td>
                        <td>Reactive and time-based maintenance are dominating maintenance strategies.</td>
                        <td>Reduces time, expense and downtime through real-time monitoring and predictive maintenance.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Lack of data acquisition systems and real-time data from assets.</td>
                        <td>Enables predictive maintenance by monitoring using systems with real-time data.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Every moment of unplanned, reactive downtime is costly, and the lack of visibility into the condition of assets is a major risk.</td>
                        <td>Helps determine the optimal way for these assets to behave and allows for proactive intervention.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Performed separately across sites or geographies often leading to inconsistent maintenance practices and systems.</td>
                        <td>Enables a unified approach to asset management across all sites.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Isolated from other business planning functions</td>
                        <td></td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
