                        <th style="width: 40%;">Benefits of technological approach</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>2.2.4 Dealing with an aging, difficult-to-replace workforce</td>
                        <td>More than third of the industry relies on human intelligence to optimize its value chain.</td>
                        <td>Expedites execution thereby generating higher productivity and efficiency.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Much of the workforce is retiring.</td>
                        <td>Enables the transfer of knowledge and experience to the next generation of workers.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>The skills required for modern mining operations are dispersed and often unavailable.</td>
                        <td>Promotes an optimized management set up with centralized control and remote operation capabilities.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Difficult to recruit and retain competent staff to run mining operations in remote and inhospitable locations.</td>
                        <td>Enables remote operation of mining assets, allowing for a focus on high-tech graduates by demonstrating industry focus on digitalization.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td></td>
                        <td>Newer employees have different attitudes and expectations</td>
                        <td></td>
                    </tr>
