<div class="page">
  <h3 style="font-size: 1.2em;">6.2.6 Mine operation scheduling</h3>
  <p>Another typical mining scenario which could be optimized through automation is scheduling. Let us assume that a drilling cycle has missed a blast round. In this case the disturbance is putting the production at risk. With automation the local operator has a scheduling system in his workplace and gets notified immediately. The critical area is clearly marked and the cause of the problem is identified.</p>
  <p>Operators and production management can discuss among themselves and run what-if analysis to simulate different solutions. Since all staff see the same information, they can jointly decide what actions to take.</p>
  <p>Everything is done in real-time; no need to wait until the end of the shift.</p>

