  <h3 style="font-size: 1.2em;">6.3 Collaborative production management: integrated-mine-to-port value chain operations</h3>
  <p>Automation is not new to mining, but the automation employed in mines is generally more basic than in other industries. It is often limited to simple control of motors, pumps and valves. However, the integration of data from different parts of the mine to have a large number of interdependent processes. Further, mines tend to be complex, with many different systems and systems from different suppliers. Each of these "islands" of automation can have its own data, format and interfaces, and operators and control room staff must scramble to multi-site, multi-system, multi-vendor, multi-domain to coordinate different parts of the process.</p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 1.2em;">6.3.1 Predictive asset monitoring</h3>
  <p>A modern asset optimization system can help mines to go from reactive to predictive maintenance strategies, avoiding unnecessary maintenance and reducing operating costs.</p>
  <p>Extended automation solutions such as System 800xA can integrate modern maintenance systems from suppliers such as IBM, SAP and Ellipse from Vertex.</p>

