<div class="page">
  <h3 style="font-size: 1.2em;">6.3.2 Stockyard management system</h3>
  <p>Bulk material handling facilities transport material from one of several locations such as a mine, a stockpile or a port. Material is temporarily stored in stockpiles or stock yards. Stockpiles are used in many different areas, such as mines, ports, refineries, power plants or manufacturing facilities.</p>
  <p>To increase production efficiency, optimize process output and reduce operating costs, a stockyard management system (SMS) is an integrated part of the overall automation system. It integrates with the process control system and it includes instrumentation, electrification and all the necessary data to allow the operator to make informed decisions.</p>
  <p>A SMS organizes the stockyard in real-time based on job definitions generated by production management. The SMS merges data on incoming material quantities with</p>

